<decompilertest>
<!--
    Kuna #1621: on arm64e a function that only signs, authenticates or
    strips a pointer and returns it decompiled as `void`.  AARCH64.pspec
    leaves the ShowPAC context at 0, and every ShowPAC=0 "hide" constructor
    in AARCH64_base_PACoptions.sinc had an empty body: `pacda x0,x16` wrote
    nothing, so x0 had no definition at the `ret` and return recovery
    found no result.  The signing was the function's only write to x0.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 p-code lift (AArch64 spec-fix, no option).  With
    ShowPAC=0 the decompiler models every signed pointer as already
    authenticated, so a hidden pac*/aut*/xpac* that writes a general
    register is now a pass-through copy of that register (Rd = Rd); the
    x30/sp and branch forms stay empty.  The signed value flows to the
    return and the store.

    First chunk: the issue's clang -O2 bytes (arm64e-apple-ios16.0):
      call_it       mov x2,x0; mov x0,x1; braaz x2
      sign_it       mov x16,x1; movk x16,#0x1234,lsl #48; pacda x0,x16; ret
      auth_it       autda x16,x17 + the FPAC-less check (xpacd, cmp, brk
                    #0xc472); mov x0,x16; ret
      strip_it      xpaci x0; ret
      sign_fn       paciza x0; ret
      store_signed  mov x16,x0; movk x16,#7,lsl #48; pacda x1,x16;
                    str x1,[x0]; ret
    Second chunk, hand-assembled, one per remaining form:
      sign_ia_plain pacia x0,x1; ret      auth_ib_plain  autib x0,x1; ret
      auth_iza      autiza x0; ret        strip_data     xpacd x0; ret
      sign_db_store pacdb x1,x0; str x1,[x0]; ret

    Before the fix sign_it, strip_it, sign_fn, sign_ia_plain,
    auth_ib_plain, auth_iza and strip_data were all `void f(void)`.
-->
